From 4e3ab05103616d9af775fb1b8a137eb50a420151 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Avery Felts <averyfelts@aol.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:34:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 27/27] FEXCore, Arm64EC: Support x86 instruction breakpoints
 in debug registers

Protectors such as Overwatch's loader set hardware breakpoints on their own
code (Dr0-3 and Dr7, from SetThreadContext or an exception handler's context)
and expect EXCEPTION_SINGLE_STEP when one is reached. FEX had no debug
registers, so the breakpoints never fired.

Each thread now keeps Dr0-3, Dr6 and Dr7 in its state. Wine's ARM64EC context
conversion has nowhere to keep them, so Wine passes the x64 context's debug
registers to FEX on NtContinue, NtSetContextThread and NtGetContextThread
(MetalSharpSetDebugRegisters and MetalSharpGetDebugRegisters), and FEX fills
them into exception contexts. Registers set on a thread before it starts in
FEX are applied when it does.

Debug registers belong to a thread while translated code is shared, so
instructions at an address any thread has an instruction breakpoint on are
compiled with a check of the running thread's enabled breakpoints. A hit
raises #DB before the instruction runs, with its bit in Dr6, unless RF in the
continued context lets it run once. Code translated before the breakpoint was
set is dropped, and the disk cache is not used while breakpoints exist.

Based on FEX-Emu/FEX#6045, whose ARM64EC part was left disabled.
